{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-172649",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "Notice that the sets are overlapping since\n\n$$\n\\{1,2,3\\}\\cap \\{0,2\\}=\\{2\\}\\ne ∅.\n$$\n\nSo for each of our sets, we form the associated set, where each element is tagged with the corresponding index, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {A}_{1} &  & \\,\\to \\, &  & {A}_{1}^{∗}=\\{(1,1),(2,1),(3,1)\\} \\\\  & {A}_{2} &  & \\,\\to \\, &  & {A}_{2}^{∗}=\\{(0,2),(2,2)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the disjoint union of our sets is simply the union of the associated tagged sets:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1}⊔{A}_{2} & =\\{1,2,3\\}⊔\\{0,2\\} \\\\  & ={A}_{1}^{∗}\\cup {A}_{2}^{∗} \\\\  & =\\{(1,1),(2,1),(3,1)\\}\\cup \\{(0,2),(2,2)\\} \\\\  & =\\{(1,1),(2,1),(3,1),(0,2),(2,2)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
